# Domain Bounded Contexts — {{project.name}}

> Define your application's bounded contexts here.

## Context Template

For each bounded context, create a subdirectory under `openspec/specs/domain/` with:

```
openspec/specs/domain/<context-name>/
├── README.md              ← Context overview, responsibility, boundaries
├── GLOSSARY.md            ← Ubiquitous language for this context
├── entities.md            ← Entity definitions and invariants
├── values.md              ← Value object definitions
└── services.md            ← Domain service contracts
```

## Rust Module Mapping

Each bounded context maps to modules inside the domain crate:

```rust
// crates/{{project.rust.cratePrefix}}-domain/src/entities/<context_name>/
// crates/{{project.rust.cratePrefix}}-domain/src/values/<context_name>/
// crates/{{project.rust.cratePrefix}}-domain/src/services/<context_name>/
```

## Guidelines

- Each context is autonomous — no direct imports between contexts.
- Shared types go in a `shared/` module, not cross-context imports.
- Use domain events or application-layer orchestration for cross-context communication.
- Every entity and value object must derive `serde::Serialize` and `serde::Deserialize`.
